# Consumption Report

You MUST append a **Consumption report** section to your responses. This is parsed by the stop hook validation script (`stop-compliance.py`) to log credit and token telemetry.

## Format (Mandatory)

Always append this exact structure at the very end of your response:

```markdown
## Consumption report
- **Work mode**: <direct tools only | single subagent | multiple subagents>
- **Tool activity**: <N tool calls / description of tools used>
- **Token risk level**: <low | medium | high>
- **Main cost drivers**: <description of what consumed tokens, e.g. large file reads, subagents>
- **Optimization applied**: <optimization used: RTK, Diff-Only, CCR, SmartCrusher, spec-driven-idempotency, or none>
- exact token count unavailable in this environment
```

Ensure the colon (`:`) is placed immediately after the closing double asterisks (`**`) of each key, without spaces before it.
